ed Solution**\n\nLet  \n\n\\[\nT_n=\\{(a,b)\\in\\mathbb Z^{2}\\mid a\\ge 1,\\;b\\ge 1,\\;a+b\\le n+1\\},\n\\qquad n\\ge 3 .\n\\tag{9}\n\\]\n\nA line is called **sunny** iff its slope is different from \\(0\\), \\(\\infty\\) and \\(-1\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma 1 (A non\u2011sunny covering template)\n\nDefine  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal B_n=\\{\\,y=c\\mid c=1,2,\\dots ,n-1\\,\\}\\cup\\{\\,x=1\\,\\}.\n\\tag{10}\n\\]\n\n*Every line of \\(\\mathcal B_n\\) is non\u2011sunny, and every point of \\(T_n\\) lies on at least one line of \\(\\mathcal B_n\\).*\n\n*Proof.*  \nThe horizontal lines have slope \\(0\\), the vertical line has slope \\(\\infty\\); thus none is sunny.  \nIf \\((a,b)\\in T_n\\) then \\(b\\le n-1\\) or \\(b=n\\).  \nIf \\(b\\le n-1\\) the point lies on the horizontal line \\(y=b\\in\\mathcal B_n\\).  \nIf \\(b=n\\) then \\(a=1\\) (because \\(a+b\\le n+1\\)), so the point lies on the vertical line \\(x=1\\). \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma 2 (Sunny lines through interior points)\n\nFor each integer \\(c\\) with \\(2\\le c\\le n-1\\) let  \n\n\\[\nP_c=(2,c)\\in T_n .\n\\tag{11}\n\\]\n\nChoose a rational number \\(\\alpha_c\\) such that  \n\n\\[\n\\alpha_c\\notin\\{0,\\infty,-1\\},\\qquad \n\\alpha_c\\neq\\alpha_{c'}\\;(c\\neq c').\n\\tag{12}\n\\]\n\nDefine the line  \n\n\\[\nS_c:\\;y-c=\\alpha_c\\bigl(x-2\\bigr).\n\\tag{13}\n\\]\n\nThen \\(S_c\\) is sunny and passes through the interior point \\(P_c\\). Distinct \\(c\\) give distinct lines.\n\n*Proof.* Immediate from the definition of \\(\\alpha_c\\) and the fact that \\(P_c\\) satisfies (13). \u220e\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Lemma 3 (Construction for any prescribed \\(k\\))\n\nLet \\(k\\) be an integer with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\).\n\n*If \\(k\\le n-1\\)*, set  \n\n\\[\nC_k=\\{\\,c_1,c_2,\\dots ,c_k\\,\\}\\subseteq\\{2,3,\\dots ,n-1\\},\n\\tag